    "outlier_investigation": {
      "question": "p6-docfix sampled 9 independent measurements of the same shipped config (boost=0.0) and found the original baseline_boost_0.0 (built ~20:22, session_count=224/episode_count=3360/chunk_count=5957) an outlier: overall MRR 0.5582 and exact-identifier MRR 0.9259, both 5-6x the noise floor above every other sample (model_ab, chunking_ab, noise-floor replicates, all built 20:36-20:52 against a larger, later corpus). Two hypotheses: (1) corpus growth over time -- more indexed content competing for top ranks decays MRR, the newest artifact should be canonical; (2) a real builder difference between eval/harness.py and model_ab.py/chunking_ab.py -- would mean eval numbers are not comparable across scripts, undermining every cross-experiment comparison made this session.",
      "discriminating_test": "Regenerated the baseline via eval/harness.py's own CLI (the exact same builder as the original 20:22 run), on the current corpus, at 21:29. Result: exact-identifier MRR = 0.8611 -- matches hypothesis 1's prediction (~0.86, the cluster every other sample sits in), not hypothesis 2's (staying near 0.926).",
