      "floor_correction": "Separately: the original baseline and model_ab's base-8M arm measure the identical config ~30 minutes apart and differ by 0.0162 on overall MRR -- above the \u00b10.012 cross-experiment floor derived from tighter, ~9-minute replicate spreads. Now that hypothesis 1 is confirmed, this 0.0162/30-min figure is real, measured corpus-growth drift, not noise to be explained away -- it is a BETTER (more conservative) floor estimate for comparisons where the time gap is unknown or could be large, and the four documents citing \u00b10.012 should probably cite something closer to this instead. See eval/results/noise_floor_2026-07-27.json's floors.mrr block, updated alongside this file."
